From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:37:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: keep BCM4388 receive DMA buffers readable too

On a MacBook Pro M4 Pro (BCM4388, PCI ID 0x4434) Wi-Fi scans, but
authentication times out, then every firmware command does ("Timeout
on response for query command"), and Bluetooth behind the same DART
times out as well. The PCIe DART takes a fault from the chip just
before.

Since commit f0ba5fd51ff2 ("wifi: brcmfmac: Set DMA direction for
msgbuf packet IDs") receive buffers are mapped DMA_FROM_DEVICE, which
permission-enforcing IOMMUs such as the Apple DART make write-only.
Commit 25836bde7a3a ("wifi: brcmfmac: Keep BCM4387 receive DMA buffers
readable") keeps them bidirectional for the BCM4387, whose firmware
reads posted receive buffers. The BCM4388 firmware does the same:
without that commit, or with this change, the same machine
associates and never faults.

Match the BCM4388 as well.

Fixes: f0ba5fd51ff2 ("wifi: brcmfmac: Set DMA direction for msgbuf packet IDs")
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c  | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
index 7db5523c83..2b1aae4ab0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -335,10 +335,11 @@ static void brcmf_msgbuf_rxbuf_ioctlresp_post(struct brcmf_msgbuf *msgbuf);
 
 
 /*
- * BCM4387 firmware can read buffers posted for receive. Since the packet-ID
- * direction is now honored, DMA_FROM_DEVICE makes those buffers write-only
- * on permission-enforcing IOMMUs. Keep RX data, event and ioctl-response
- * buffers readable, with the same direction used for mapping and unmapping.
+ * BCM4387 and BCM4388 firmware can read buffers posted for receive. Since
+ * the packet-ID direction is now honored, DMA_FROM_DEVICE makes those
+ * buffers write-only on permission-enforcing IOMMUs. Keep RX data, event and
+ * ioctl-response buffers readable, with the same direction used for mapping
+ * and unmapping.
  */
 static enum dma_data_direction
 brcmf_msgbuf_rx_dma_direction(struct device *dev)
@@ -350,8 +351,9 @@ brcmf_msgbuf_rx_dma_direction(struct device *dev)
 
 	pdev = to_pci_dev(dev);
 	if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_BROADCOM &&
-	    pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4387_DEVICE_ID) {
-		dev_info(dev, "BCM4387: using bidirectional receive DMA\n");
+	    (pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4387_DEVICE_ID ||
+	     pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4388_DEVICE_ID)) {
+		dev_info(dev, "using bidirectional receive DMA\n");
 		return DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL;
 	}
 
